From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:31:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: claim PCI id 0x110e

The OnePlus 13 radio enumerates as 17cb:110e. Claim it on the
WCN7850 path so the SOC version can be read. On this phone that
read reports major 0xf, and the probe returns before firmware.

Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index 1f3cfd9b8..0f7853f1f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -40,6 +40,10 @@
 
 #define QCN9274_DEVICE_ID		0x1109
 #define WCN7850_DEVICE_ID		0x1107
+/* OnePlus 13 (peach) enumerates as this id after the 7850 power
+ * sequence. The SOC version below decides whether the 7850 ops fit.
+ */
+#define WCN7850_PEACH_DEVICE_ID		0x110e
 
 #define PCIE_LOCAL_REG_QRTR_NODE_ID	0x1E03164
 #define DOMAIN_NUMBER_MASK		GENMASK(7, 4)
@@ -48,6 +52,7 @@
 static const struct pci_device_id ath12k_pci_id_table[] = {
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(QCOM, QCN9274_DEVICE_ID) },
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(QCOM, WCN7850_DEVICE_ID) },
+	{ PCI_VDEVICE(QCOM, WCN7850_PEACH_DEVICE_ID) },
 	{0}
 };
 
@@ -1611,6 +1616,7 @@ static int ath12k_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 		}
 		break;
 	case WCN7850_DEVICE_ID:
+	case WCN7850_PEACH_DEVICE_ID:
 		ab->id.bdf_search = ATH12K_BDF_SEARCH_BUS_AND_BOARD;
 		ab_pci->msi_config = &ath12k_msi_config[0];
 		ab->static_window_map = false;
-- 
2.55.0

